    <div class="view library-view">
      <div class="quick-add-row">
        <input type="text" class="quick-add-input" placeholder="Paste a YouTube link to queue it right now…" autocomplete="off" />
        <button type="button" class="btn quick-add-btn">+ Queue it</button>
      </div>

      <div class="search-row">
        <input type="text" class="search-input" placeholder="Search singer or song title…" />
        <div class="sort-toggle">
          <button data-sort="singer" class="on">Singer</button>
          <button data-sort="song">Song</button>
          <button data-sort="history">History</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="disconnected-hint hidden">Connect to a Stage above to see its song library.</div>
      <div class="song-list"></div>

      <section class="quickstart hidden" aria-label="Quick start">
        <div class="qs-eyebrow">Quick start</div>
        <h2 class="qs-lead">To start karaoke, you need a <span class="qs-chip">Stage</span> running.</h2>
        <p class="qs-lead-sub">The Stage is the host: it plays the songs, and everything else connects to it. Keep its tab open while you sing.</p>

        <ol class="qs-steps">
          <li class="qs-step">
            <span class="qs-num">1</span>
            <div class="qs-step-body">
              <h3>Open the Stage</h3>
              <p>Tap <span class="qs-chip">Stage ⛶</span> at the top. It opens in a new tab — put it on your TV or big screen, then tap <b>Tap to start the show</b>.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="qs-step">
            <span class="qs-num">2</span>
            <div class="qs-step-body">
              <h3>Connect a device</h3>
              <p>On any phone, tablet or laptop, <b>scan the QR code</b> shown on the Stage. That device becomes a client where you add and remove songs.</p>
              <p class="qs-alt">No camera? Tap the connect button at the top right and type the room code.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="qs-notes">
          <div class="qs-notes-title">Good to know</div>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <b>Adding songs.</b> Paste a YouTube link into <i>Queue it</i> above, or bulk-import from ⚙ Settings → Import Songs.
              You can also use <b>https links to your own media files</b> (the file server must allow CORS).
              Only those local CORS links support <b>key change</b> — YouTube songs don't.
              An iPhone/iPad used as the Stage doesn't work with CORS links, so use YouTube there.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Same Wi-Fi.</b> The Stage and every client device need to be on the same Wi-Fi to connect —
              unless you've set up a TURN / STUN server (⚙ Settings → TURN / STUN Server).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
